  {
   "sc": 8,
   "shot": "8.1",
   "start": 413.11,
   "end": 438.14,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "It's a box. With nothing in it. They are paying two hundred dollars for air.",
     "start": 413.11,
     "end": 419.16
    },
    {
     "who": "BEV",
     "text": "Not air, honey. Air's got stuff in it.",
     "start": 419.28,
     "end": 422.81
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "I'm the only sane person in this town.",
     "start": 422.93,
     "end": 426.46
    },
    {
     "who": "BEV",
     "text": "Everybody who's ever sat on that stool said that exact thing.",
     "start": 426.58,
     "end": 431.19
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "Were they right?",
     "start": 431.31,
     "end": 433.04
    },
    {
     "who": "BEV",
     "text": "One was. He moved to Omaha. Now he's insane in Omaha.",
     "start": 433.16,
     "end": 438.02
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 8,
   "shot": "8.2",
   "start": 438.14,
   "end": 461.75,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "BEV",
     "text": "I've watched this town buy every dumb thing you can name. You know what none of 'em were buying?",
     "start": 438.14,
     "end": 445.63
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "The thing.",
     "start": 445.75,
     "end": 447.12
    },
    {
     "who": "BEV",
     "text": "Bein' first. Bein' in on it. You can't put that in a box, so they put nothing in a box and said \"that's it.\" And it is.",
     "start": 447.24,
     "end": 456.24
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "That's the stupidest thing I've ever heard.",
     "start": 456.36,
     "end": 459.53
    },
    {
     "who": "BEV",
     "text": "On the house.",
     "start": 459.65,
     "end": 461.63
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 8,
   "shot": "8.3",
   "start": 461.75,
   "end": 467.65,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "…I'm not going to open it.",
     "start": 463.35,
     "end": 466.16
    },
    {
     "who": "BEV",
     "text": "Sure.",
     "start": 466.28,
     "end": 467.53
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 9,
   "shot": "9.1",
   "start": 467.65,
   "end": 471.25,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 9,
   "shot": "9.2",
   "start": 471.25,
   "end": 473.65,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 9,
   "shot": "9.3",
   "start": 473.65,
   "end": 477.59,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "…Oh, no.",
     "start": 475.05,
     "end": 476.67
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 9,
   "shot": "9.4",
   "start": 477.59,
   "end": 479.39,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 9,
   "shot": "9.5",
   "start": 479.39,
   "end": 482.39,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 10,
   "shot": "10.1",
   "start": 482.39,
   "end": 490.99,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "People ask me… \"Dex… what is VOID?\"",
     "start": 482.39,
     "end": 486.29
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "And I tell them…",
     "start": 486.41,
     "end": 489.06
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "…nothing.",
     "start": 489.18,
     "end": 490.87
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 10,
   "shot": "10.2",
   "start": 490.99,
   "end": 493.99,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 10,
   "shot": "10.3",
   "start": 493.99,
   "end": 518.59,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "GORDY",
     "text": "Kenzie. People think VOID is hiding something. There's a forum. They think the boxes are \"empty on purpose\" because the real thing is too dangerous to ship.",
     "start": 493.99,
     "end": 502.99
    },
    {
     "who": "KENZIE",
     "text": "I'm at nine hundred and ninety-one thousand. I'm nine thousand from a million. Gordy, I need you to say \"they don't want you to have it\" one more time on camera.",
     "start": 503.11,
     "end": 512.36
    },
    {
     "who": "GORDY",
     "text": "I don't think I believe it anymore.",
     "start": 512.48,
     "end": 515.65
    },
    {
     "who": "KENZIE",
     "text": "That's even better, say that.",
     "start": 515.77,
     "end": 518.47
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 10,
   "shot": "10.4",
   "start": 518.59,
   "end": 536.01,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "Pruitt Principle number one: less is more.",
     "start": 518.59,
     "end": 521.76
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "Pruitt Principle number two: nothing… is everything.",
     "start": 521.88,
     "end": 525.05
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "And Pruitt Principle number forty—",
     "start": 525.17,
     "end": 527.62
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN (O.S.)",
     "text": "You can't skip to forty.",
     "start": 527.74,
     "end": 530.44
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "—is that one day, every box in America will be a VOID box.",
     "start": 530.56,
     "end": 535.89
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 10,
   "shot": "10.5",
   "start": 536.01,
   "end": 563.91,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "Quick correction, Dex.",
     "start": 536.01,
     "end": 537.74
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "As of 8:14 this morning, VOID is a registered trademark of Feld Holdings, LLC. A Delaware company.",
     "start": 537.86,
     "end": 544.88
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "You trademarked nothing?",
     "start": 545,
     "end": 546.98
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "It's Delaware. You can trademark anything.",
     "start": 547.1,
     "end": 549.91
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "We're co-founders!",
     "start": 550.03,
     "end": 551.4
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "You're a founder. I'm the owner. It's different. Look it up.",
     "start": 551.52,
     "end": 556.13
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "I was going to put you in my memoir!",
     "start": 556.25,
     "end": 560.14
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "Chapter one is going to be really short.",
     "start": 560.26,
     "end": 563.79
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 10,
   "shot": "10.6",
   "start": 563.91,
   "end": 575.13,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "PRINCIPAL GAINES",
     "text": "Okay! Okay. Here's my ruling. There will be two VOID drops. Team Pruitt. And Team Feld. Saturday, ValuBarn. And then this school never speaks of it again.",
     "start": 563.91,
     "end": 572.91
    },
    {
     "who": "PRINCIPAL GAINES",
     "text": "That's a ruling.",
     "start": 573.03,
     "end": 575.01
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 10,
   "shot": "10.7",
   "start": 575.13,
   "end": 577.59,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "KENZIE",
     "text": "Come on… come on…",
     "start": 575.13,
     "end": 577.47
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 10,
   "shot": "10.8",
   "start": 577.59,
   "end": 588.07,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "YOUNGER KID",
     "text": "Oh my gosh. Are you the VOID girl?",
     "start": 577.59,
     "end": 581.12
    },
    {
     "who": "KENZIE",
     "text": "I am the VOID girl.",
     "start": 581.24,
     "end": 583.94
    },
    {
     "who": "YOUNGER KID",
     "text": "Can you get me a picture with your sister?",
     "start": 584.06,
     "end": 587.95
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 10,
   "shot": "10.9",
   "start": 588.07,
   "end": 590.47,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.1",
   "start": 590.47,
   "end": 593.47,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.2",
   "start": 593.47,
   "end": 602.04,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "Who should I make it out to?",
     "start": 593.47,
     "end": 596.89
    },
    {
     "who": "CUSTOMER",
     "text": "Just sign \"nothing.\"",
     "start": 597.01,
     "end": 598.74
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "Love that. That's a Pruitt Principle.",
     "start": 598.86,
     "end": 601.92
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.3",
   "start": 602.04,
   "end": 612.99,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "VOID Prime is two-fifty. VOID Prime Plus is three-ten. Plus means you get the lid.",
     "start": 602.04,
     "end": 608.09
    },
    {
     "who": "CUSTOMER 2",
     "text": "The other one didn't have a lid?",
     "start": 608.21,
     "end": 611.38
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "Not legally.",
     "start": 611.5,
     "end": 612.87
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.4",
   "start": 612.99,
   "end": 615.81,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "SHAKING MAN",
     "text": "There's something in this one.",
     "start": 612.99,
     "end": 615.69
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.5",
   "start": 615.81,
   "end": 624.44,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "GORDY",
     "text": "No. No, no, no, there isn't, I made that up, it's a theory—",
     "start": 615.81,
     "end": 621.14
    },
    {
     "who": "SHAKING MAN",
     "text": "THIS ONE HAS THE REAL THING!",
     "start": 621.26,
     "end": 624.32
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.6",
   "start": 624.44,
   "end": 626.84,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.7",
   "start": 626.84,
   "end": 628.64,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.8",
   "start": 628.64,
   "end": 631.04,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.9",
   "start": 631.04,
   "end": 639.74,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "KENZIE",
     "text": "You guys, this is literally the best day of my life—",
     "start": 631.04,
     "end": 635.9
    },
    {
     "who": "KENZIE",
     "text": "Ow.",
     "start": 636.02,
     "end": 637.52
    },
    {
     "who": "KENZIE",
     "text": "—and it's raw!",
     "start": 637.64,
     "end": 639.62
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.10",
   "start": 639.74,
   "end": 649.11,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "OFFICER MALLORY",
     "text": "We've got a fire at ValuBarn and a riot over empty boxes. Send everybody. And open the DMV, I'm gonna need the holding cell.",
     "start": 639.74,
     "end": 648.99
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.11",
   "start": 649.11,
   "end": 652.4,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "MAYOR KRUPP",
     "text": "I'd like to officially open this riot—",
     "start": 649.11,
     "end": 652.28
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.12",
   "start": 652.4,
   "end": 658.54,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "TUNK",
     "text": "Needed it.",
     "start": 655.8,
     "end": 657.42
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.13",
   "start": 658.54,
   "end": 668.05,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "This is your fault!",
     "start": 658.54,
     "end": 660.63
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "My fault? You told a gym that nothing is everything!",
     "start": 660.75,
     "end": 665
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "It is everything! Look at it!",
     "start": 665.12,
     "end": 667.93
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.14",
   "start": 668.05,
   "end": 670.65,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.15",
   "start": 670.65,
   "end": 684.39,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "KENZIE",
     "text": "Not Wren Okafor being a VOID-head.",
     "start": 670.65,
     "end": 673.71
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "I can explain.",
     "start": 673.83,
     "end": 675.81
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "I can't explain.",
     "start": 675.93,
     "end": 677.91
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "You said no! It's on the record!",
     "start": 678.03,
     "end": 681.45
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "I know what I said!",
     "start": 681.57,
     "end": 684.27
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.16",
   "start": 684.39,
   "end": 686.19,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.17",
   "start": 686.19,
   "end": 688.79,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 11,
   "shot": "11.18",
   "start": 688.79,
   "end": 701.79,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "FRINK",
     "text": "Thank you, everyone. That will be all.",
     "start": 689.79,
     "end": 693.21
    },
    {
     "who": "FRINK",
     "text": "You six. Come with me.",
     "start": 693.33,
     "end": 696.03
    },
    {
     "who": "GORDY",
     "text": "I'm not saying it's connected.",
     "start": 696.15,
     "end": 698.85
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "Gordy, it is so connected.",
     "start": 698.97,
     "end": 701.67
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 12,
   "shot": "12.1",
   "start": 701.79,
   "end": 707.83,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "FRINK",
     "text": "Help yourselves.",
     "start": 701.79,
     "end": 703.16
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "Are we getting the forty dollars?",
     "start": 703.28,
     "end": 706.09
    },
    {
     "who": "FRINK",
     "text": "No.",
     "start": 706.21,
     "end": 707.71
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 12,
   "shot": "12.2",
   "start": 707.83,
   "end": 744.71,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "FRINK",
     "text": "In eleven days, you sold three hundred and eight thousand units of an empty box. You created a national cardboard shortage. You triggered a riot in a superstore over the rumor of contents. With ninety-four percent confidence, you have proven the single most valuable consumer finding in the history of my company.",
     "start": 707.83,
     "end": 716.83
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "That nothing… is everything?",
     "start": 716.95,
     "end": 719.29
    },
    {
     "who": "FRINK",
     "text": "That Americans will buy nothing, if it's scarce, and someone tells them they can't have it.",
     "start": 719.41,
     "end": 725.82
    },
    {
     "who": "GORDY",
     "text": "I'm the someone.",
     "start": 725.94,
     "end": 727.92
    },
    {
     "who": "FRINK",
     "text": "You were very effective.",
     "start": 728.04,
     "end": 730.13
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "Okay. Great. So let's talk licensing, because I own the VOID trademark—",
     "start": 730.25,
     "end": 735.22
    },
    {
     "who": "FRINK",
     "text": "You signed the Median Participation Agreement at birth. Section Forty, Subsection C. Any product invented within town limits is the property of the test.",
     "start": 735.34,
     "end": 744.59
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 12,
   "shot": "12.3",
   "start": 744.71,
   "end": 753.75,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "This is… really good contract work.",
     "start": 744.71,
     "end": 747.77
    },
    {
     "who": "FRINK",
     "text": "Thank you. I wrote it in 1988.",
     "start": 747.89,
     "end": 751.06
    },
    {
     "who": "KENZIE",
     "text": "So what happens to VOID?",
     "start": 751.18,
     "end": 753.63
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 12,
   "shot": "12.4",
   "start": 753.75,
   "end": 760.91,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "AD ANNOUNCER (V.O.)",
     "text": "Introducing VOID+. Nothing. Delivered monthly. Fourteen ninety-nine. Cancel anytime.",
     "start": 754.55,
     "end": 758.69
    },
    {
     "who": "AD ANNOUNCER (V.O.)",
     "text": "Cancellation not available.",
     "start": 758.81,
     "end": 760.79
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 12,
   "shot": "12.5",
   "start": 760.91,
   "end": 763.51,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 12,
   "shot": "12.6",
   "start": 763.51,
   "end": 782.98,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "So we invented a way for a corporation to charge people for nothing.",
     "start": 764.71,
     "end": 770.04
    },
    {
     "who": "GORDY",
     "text": "To be fair, they were already doing that. We just gave it a box.",
     "start": 770.16,
     "end": 775.85
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "Can we… at least be in the commercial?",
     "start": 775.97,
     "end": 779.75
    },
    {
     "who": "FRINK",
     "text": "No.",
     "start": 779.87,
     "end": 781.12
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "That's fair.",
     "start": 781.24,
     "end": 782.86
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 13,
   "shot": "13.1",
   "start": 782.98,
   "end": 785.58,
   "lines": []
  },
  {
   "sc": 13,
   "shot": "13.2",
   "start": 785.58,
   "end": 797.73,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "KENZIE",
     "text": "Cool. Cool cool cool.",
     "start": 788.38,
     "end": 790.72
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "Maybe… the real product… was the friends we—",
     "start": 790.84,
     "end": 794.62
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS, WREN, KENZIE, GORDY",
     "text": "Don't.",
     "start": 794.74,
     "end": 796.24
    },
    {
     "who": "DEX",
     "text": "Okay.",
     "start": 796.36,
     "end": 797.61
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 13,
   "shot": "13.3",
   "start": 797.73,
   "end": 813.02,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "Your loan. Plus twelve percent.",
     "start": 797.73,
     "end": 800.18
    },
    {
     "who": "TUNK",
     "text": "Hill'll be glad.",
     "start": 800.3,
     "end": 802.28
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "You paid him back? With interest?",
     "start": 802.4,
     "end": 805.46
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "He fronted us. You pay back people who front you.",
     "start": 805.58,
     "end": 810.08
    },
    {
     "who": "MARCUS",
     "text": "It's good for my credit.",
     "start": 810.2,
     "end": 812.9
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "sc": 13,
   "shot": "13.4",
   "start": 813.02,
   "end": 820.21,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "GORDY",
     "text": "Why'd you buy thirty?",
     "start": 813.02,
     "end": 815.11
    },
    {
     "who": "WREN",
     "text": "It was nice. Opening it. Wanting nothing. For, like, a minute.",
